# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LumaWall repository
#
# Principle: only source, the marketing site, and the reusable tools are
# tracked. Build output, captured frames, exploratory scripts, sample media and
# installers are all regenerable, and installers are published as GitHub
# Releases instead (they are ~40 MB per version; committing them would add that
# to every clone forever).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── build output ──
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
msix/verify/
msix/stage/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.prelegacy.bak

# ── generated during development ──
build/
outputs/
installer/Output/
*.log

# ── installers ──
# These were ignored on the reasoning that they are "published as Releases, never
# committed". That was wrong for this project: the site links to
# site/assets/downloads/LumaWall-Setup-4.0.1.exe, so the files have to be in the
# deploy. Ignoring them meant every download on the live site returned 404 while the
# files sat on this machine - the site looked finished and could not be installed
# from. 42 MB of installers is the point of a download page.
#
# The pattern is scoped to the site's own folder; a stray .exe elsewhere (a build
# artefact, a test binary) is still ignored.
*.exe
!tools/FullscreenCover.exe
!site/assets/downloads/*.exe
*.msi
*.msix
!site/assets/downloads/*.msix
site/assets/downloads/*.zip
!site/assets/downloads/*.zip

# ── wallpaper library (user content, not source) ──
LumaWall/assets/*
!LumaWall/assets/.gitkeep

# ── development scratch at the repository root ──
# Every file below was part of exploring the logo, capturing frames, testing
# media handling, or iterating on the UI. None of it is needed to build or
# understand LumaWall, and it is all regenerable.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.mp4
/*.ico
/logo_*.py
/explore_logo*.py
/patch_icons*.py
/diag_icon.py
/fix_manifest_paths.py
/build_mature_contact_sheets.py
/build_*catalog*.ps1
/build_dynamic_loops.ps1
/apply_mature_audit.ps1
/create-brand.ps1
/capture_window.ps1
/decode-ab.ps1
/detector-test.ps1
/fullscreen-test.ps1
/hook-proof.ps1
/inspect-desktop.ps1
/lock-test*.ps1
/maximized-test*.ps1
/measure-decode.ps1
/pause-probe.ps1
/pause-test*.ps1
/perf-state.ps1
/probe-windows.ps1
/resume-latency.ps1
/test_flicker*.ps1
/test_loop_seam.ps1
/test-animation.ps1

# ── scratch directories ──
/catalog_sources/
/mature-audit/
/loop-bases/
/reference/
/archive/
/backup-*/
/store-art/
/single-instance-test-*/
/packages/

# ── OS noise ──
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── leftovers from development ──
LumaWall/*.bak
LumaWall/fps-test-*.mp4
tools/render-DISPLAY*.png
tools/FullscreenCover.exe

# ── signing material ──
# The .pfx holds a private key. Only the public .cer belongs in the repository,
# and even that is a development certificate - the Store re-signs the package
# with the publisher's own certificate during submission.
msix/*.pfx
msix/*.pvk
msix/*.snk
*.pfx

# ── promo video renderer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The promo is built from source (promo/src) plus the real product assets in
# site/assets. node_modules and the vite output are build products, and dist
# contains a full copy of the site's assets (62 MB) that would duplicate what is
# already tracked under site/.
promo/node_modules/
promo/dist/
promo/package-lock.json

.vercel

# Wallpaper frame sequences for the promo renderer: 13 MB of intermediate data
# regenerated by tools/extract-clips.py, never deployed and never served.
promo/frames/

# The raw 720p clips were replaced by the frame sequences above.
site/assets/video/clips/

# A render in progress writes here; it must never be committed or deployed.
*.part.mp4
site/assets/video/*.part.mp4

# esbuild on Windows writes its /dev/null equivalent into the working directory.
promo/dev/
